# The claim's durable entry write is a plain write, refused only against the
# loaded entry. Two overlapping claims write out of order, the lower epoch lands
# last, and after a WAL shard restart the entry reloads below the epoch the
# newer claim raised, readmitting the superseded activation.
MODULE: StaleEpochNeverAppendsClaimEntryOverwrite
TARGET: StaleEpochNeverAppends
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the claim overwrites the durable entry instead of max-merging it
PERTURBS: ClaimWrite
BOUNDS: WithRestart = TRUE, WithBatch = FALSE, MaxWindows = 1

--- FIND
    /\ epoch[a] > Max2(Max2(fence, memFence), retired)
    /\ fence' = Max2(fence, epoch[a])
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a plain write, checked against the loaded entry only.
    /\ epoch[a] > Max2(memFence, retired)
    /\ fence' = epoch[a]
--- END
